From 4ed849e326793ec06862c283da63bdcee523e2df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:27:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ex7, ex8: fixes of an independent review of the direct solver
 options

- ex8: the long names of the options no longer refer to MUMPS
  (--matrix-symmetry-mechanics for -msMc, --reuse-analysis for -mra), as
  in ex7; the fields of the options are renamed accordingly; an invalid
  symmetry is refused right after the parsing with a message naming the
  option (no backtrace); -mra is ignored with a warning when no direct
  solver is used; comments updated;
- ex8 README: rows of -msMc and -mra (both direct solvers, heat transfer
  and elastic operator of NewtonK0, figures of MUMPS and of cuDSS), GPU
  example with the behaviour libraries of the generic-parallel interface
  (-lU, -lA) and a baseline with the same options (9.7 s with MUMPS and
  BoomerAMG on the host, 2.6 s with cuDSS);
- ex7: -ls and -ms are checked right after the parsing, whatever the
  solver, with messages naming the options; -ms and -mra are ignored with
  a warning without a direct solver, and -ls, -ms and -mra with PETSc;
- ex7 README: options -l, --device and --hypre-on-host, refusals and
  warnings, GPU command line, description of the problem;
- ex7: test mox2-mumps (MUMPS, symmetric positive definite matrices,
  compared to the same reference), registered if MFEM provides MUMPS.
---
